- [ ] **Stage 5 — proactive context compaction.**
  - Current branch: work; inspected head before Stage 5 candidate design: 022fc937b9cd681c36b1d616392296ad873a6439.
  - Stage 4 is complete and CI-verified: exact OpenAI API input-token preflight; Gemini Developer API approximate countTokens preflight; confidence-aware policy (approximate estimates never hard-block); verified model capability/context metadata; output reserve and safety headroom; shared accounting; one safe compaction/recount attempt; native tool-call pairing and canonical history preservation. Do not redo Stage 4.
  - **Completed step 1 — architecture inspection:** compaction is synchronous at the RunContext turn boundary. maybeCompactContext checks previous provider usage, and compactActiveContext copies prefix/tail, makes one summary Generate call, persists a context_snapshot, then replaces a.messages. Errors before snapshot persistence retain active context and canonical records. contextCompactionCut validates complete call/result boundaries and retains at least six tail messages; snapshots preserve NativeSteps. resumeEntry restores the latest snapshot plus canonical records after it. Session Message metadata currently carries only ContextSnapshotCount—no source boundary/version token.
    - Ownership: a.messages is mutated by RunContext, Clear, Rewind, NewSession and resumeEntry; there is no dedicated messages mutex or Agent run mutex. Normal TUI operation serializes prompts with working/submitOnEnter and only Ctrl-C can interrupt; HTTP generation routes share chatMu and wait for runDone after cancellation; scheduler/team workers use separate Agent instances. These frontend guards do not make Agent itself concurrency-safe.
    - Reads/callbacks: /context reads ContextStatus and ContextChars; ContextChars iterates a.messages without a lock. ChatMessages uses activityMu, but direct RunContext appends to chatMessages and some direct history.Add calls do not use that lock. TUI text/event sinks forward to buffered UI channels; server sinks forward to an event channel. They do not themselves mutate a.messages. Server plain GET can read ChatMessages while RunContext is running, so its current activityMu protection is incomplete.
    - Persistence/cancellation: Session.Store.Add has no internal mutex; callers currently serialize most writes. RunContext and synchronous summary share the run context, so cancellation/errors normally prevent snapshot application. Server cancellation waits for runDone; TUI cancellation waits for the done event. A future worker must not touch the live message slice or Store from its goroutine.
  - **Active step 2:** build a pure immutable compaction candidate with session path, source messages, cut boundary, revision and reset epoch; add a rebase validator that accepts only append-only tail growth and rejects changed session/epoch, rewound/replaced source prefix, or a stale cut. Add unit tests only; no goroutine, session persistence or live behavior changes yet. Then instrument active-message append/rewrite/reset paths so every mutation increments revision and destructive replacements advance epoch.
  - **Policy targets:** approximately 80% for early preparation and 95% for a safety barrier, adjusted for fixed request overhead, output reserve, estimator confidence and provider limits. These are policy targets, not hard-coded universal limits.
  - **Required invariants:** summarize only structurally complete prefixes; retain the untouched tail and all newly appended messages; canonical archive remains immutable/resumable; one summary request by default; no summary failure may abort an otherwise valid turn; no dangling artifact references.
  - **Tests:** valid cut boundaries; stale snapshot rejection/rebase; concurrent appends; cancellation/failure fallback; cooldown; snapshot resume; canonical archive equality; artifact-reference integrity.
